[VOICE]: Off

[STYLE]
Hyperreal industrial sci-fi catastrophe. Ancient rusted orbital fortress-cities, weaponized asteroids, glowing fracture cores, dense debris, ruined megastructures, vulnerable planet below. No polished sci-fi; everything old, heavy, damaged, dangerous, already failing.

[CORE]
Not natural asteroids: ancient siege weapons disguised as dead orbital debris. They wake from inside: orange engineered cracks ignite under stone, widen, vent pressure, scrape fortress-cities, fragment, and turn orbit into a collapsing mined belt. Horror = realization, not impact.

[CAMERA]
FPV survival-camera / cockpit-adjacent only. Constant survival motion: dodge wreckage, slip through gaps, avoid collisions, shoved by shockwaves. Forward drift, roll, yaw, pitch, foreground parallax, debris inches from lens. No calm camera. Tiny ships only as scale needles.

[NEGATIVE]
No cartoon, anime, painterly, cel-shade, glossy game CG. No clean dogfight. No polished white ships. No laser battle focus. No static asteroid shots. No slow motion. No freeze frames. No elegant symmetry. No fantasy glow. No cartoon explosions. No hero craft. No triumphant ending. No calm empty space.

[SCENES]

0.00–0.90
Start mid-incident. Camera rips through a dense orbital ruin corridor. Rusted towers streak past both sides. Ahead, a dead asteroid hangs between fortress spines. Thin orange cracks ignite beneath its crust.

0.90–1.80
Violent side-slip past a docking spine. Two more dead asteroids ignite deeper in frame, not exploding, only waking. Dust vents from cracks. Fortress walls flash orange.

1.80–2.80
Camera dives beneath a collapsing bridge. Above, the first weapon-stone rotates, showing glowing fracture networks like a buried reactor. Heavy chunks drift outward. Fast shrapnel whips past lens.

2.80–3.80
Near-collision with a tower edge. Whip-pan right: another asteroid scrapes a fortress needle. Stone, sparks, rusted plates, and antenna fragments burst into the corridor.

3.80–4.80
Camera punches through fresh debris. Dust blinds the view. A burning asteroid shard tumbles close to lens, glowing with engineered molten geometry inside.

4.80–5.80
Burst into a wider ruined orbital chamber. Fortress-city masses tower left. Far ahead, a weapon-stone splits along a glowing seam and vents fire sideways, correcting drift.

5.80–6.80
Hard roll to avoid shearing wreckage. Below, planet curvature appears. Above, a fortress module collapses inward as a glowing stone passes behind it.

6.80–7.80
Tiny interceptors streak across frame. One nearly crosses camera path. A huge asteroid rotates into partial view: rough crust outside, molten geometric weapon-core pulsing underneath.

7.80–8.80
Off-frame rupture. Pressure wave rolls metallic dust through the corridor. Fortress plates rip away. Camera is shoved into a narrow pass of cables, bridges, spinning debris.

8.80–9.80
Knife-thread through the pass. Wreckage flashes inches from lens. Ahead, the first major weapon-stone drifts toward a cathedral-sized defense spine. Fracture-light turns white-hot.

9.80–10.80
Near miss. The glowing stone skims the defense spine instead of striking. Contact peels a whole structural face outward. Towers break, dust rolls, chambers flash, then vanish.

10.80–11.80
Camera dives under falling slabs. Tiny ships weave through the same impossible gap. No one is fighting. Everyone is escaping.

11.80–12.80
A second weapon-stone cracks open wider, revealing an inner furnace wrapped in broken crust. Burning fragments fall away. The truth lands: the rocks were built.

12.80–13.80
Fast roll left through floating wreckage. A ruined docking mass rotates foreground while three more asteroids ignite behind it at different depths. Chain activation spreads.

13.80–15.00
Final escalation. Camera clears into a downward corridor toward the planet. Glowing debris and ruined modules fall inward. Last frame: collapsing mined belt over the planet, multiple weapon-stones awakening in depth.